#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203856 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204102 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6600adba-92a6-523c-b214-9e506bc37cc9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradients of Linear Forms"}] :question/id #uuid "8ad540bc-bc15-5b57-aa7a-1ea46693a4e0" :question/math-academy-id "e-17348" :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f: \\mathbb{R}^4 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ with respect to $\\mathbf{x}$ at $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Writing $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, we have\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x})= \\mathbf{b}^T\\mathbf{x}\n$$\n\nThe gradient of a function\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\mathbf{b}^T\\mathbf{x}\n$$\n\nwith respect to $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$ is\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n$\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203864 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204103 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7de7a9a-4848-5590-b066-f746262181e5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradients Including Squared Norms"}] :question/id #uuid "d50d20a4-2c3e-5469-8ced-2fde5d6690e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-17754" :question/problem "Given the function\n$f(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{w}) = -7\\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{x} + \\left.3\\|\\mathbf{w}\\\\right|^2 - 2$\nthat maps two vectors to a scalar, find $\\nabla_{\\mathbf w} f$." :question/worked-solution "Using the results\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf w}(\\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}, \\qquad \\nabla_{\\mathbf w} (\\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{w}) = 2\\mathbf{w}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇_{w}f &= ∇_{w}(-7w^{T}x + 3‖w‖^{2} - 2) \\\\\n&=-7 \\cdot ∇_{w}(w^{T}x) + 3 \\cdot ∇_{w}(‖w‖^{2}) - ∇_{w}(2) \\\\\n&=-7 \\cdot ∇_{w}(w^{T}x) + 3 \\cdot ∇_{w}(w^{T}w) - ∇_{w}(2) \\\\\n&=-7 \\cdot x + 3 \\cdot 2w - 0 \\\\\n&=-7x + 6w\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203874 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204104 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86b3efb7-511d-5da7-92ca-5add976b1ca1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradients of Functions Containing L1 Norms"}] :question/id #uuid "5222f4d3-4fec-545c-b9f3-4d8a8e84d2c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-18710" :question/problem "Given the function\n$f(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{w}) = \\left.-3\\left(\\|\\mathbf{w}\\\\right|_1\\right)^3 - 5\\mathbf x^T\\mathbf w$\nthat maps a vector to a scalar, find $\\nabla_{\\mathbf w}f$. You may assume that $\\mathbf w$ has no zero components." :question/worked-solution "Using the results\n\n$$\n\\left.\\nabla_{\\mathbf w} (\\|\\mathbf{w}\\\\right|_1) = \\text{sign}(\\mathbf{w}), \\qquad \\nabla_{\\mathbf w}\\left(\\mathbf x^T\\mathbf w\\right) = \\mathbf x\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇_{w}f &= ∇_{w}(-3(‖w‖_{1})^{3} - 5x^{T}w) \\\\\n&= ∇_{w}(-3(‖w‖_{1})^{3}) - ∇_{w}(5x^{T}w) \\\\\n&=-3 \\cdot ∇_{w}((‖w‖_{1})^{3}) - 5 \\cdot ∇_{w}(x^{T}w) \\\\\n&=-3 \\cdot 3(‖w‖_{1})^{2} \\cdot ∇_{w}(‖w‖_{1}) - 5 \\cdot x \\\\\n&=-3 \\cdot 3(‖w‖_{1})^{2} \\cdot sign(w) - 5 \\cdot x \\\\\n&=-9(‖w‖_{1})^{2} \\cdot sign(w) - 5x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204103 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7de7a9a-4848-5590-b066-f746262181e5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradients Including Squared Norms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8333ad5c-643c-532a-a7ae-6d46ae048983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203359} {:answer/id #uuid "96f16ea5-08aa-5ce8-982b-c204221184c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10w + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203360} {:answer/id #uuid "bf677492-92fb-553b-bf5b-66a092456cb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :a